SUMMARY:Emoji: The Hieroglyphs of Our Time\, or how I learned to stop worry
 ing and send the risky text
LOCATION:Edinburgh
DESCRIPTION:Sold out at the NYC Fringe Festival 2025. Part love letter\, pa
 rt stand-up set\, part concert and part iPhone advert (jk!)\, the show expl
 ores whether emojis are a uniquely universal shorthand or merely digital cr
 umbs of connection in a fractured society. In this hilarious\, heartfelt\, 
 ADHD-friendly show packed with energetic musical numbers\, sparkling visual
 s and audience participation\, Aarushi Agni delivers a chaotic TED Talk/mus
 ical about emoji and risky texts blending sharp comedy\, cultural insight a
 nd impressive vocal dynamism.\nMore info: https://comedyatlas.app/comedy-at
 las/event/emoji-the-hieroglyphs-of-our-time-or-how-i-learned-to-stop-worryi
